      164.49,
      203.33,
      399.2,
      227.27
    ],
    "text": "AN ACT TO AMEND THE LOCAL AUTHORITIES ELECTIONS ORDINANCENO. 53 OF 1946",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      7.0,
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      161.85,
      241.13,
      401.91,
      265.07
    ],
    "text": "BE it enacted by the Parliament of the Democratic SocialistRepublic of Sri Lanka as follows:\u2014",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      161.85,
      278.93,
      401.89,
      302.87
    ],
    "text": "1.This Act may be cited as the Local AuthoritiesElections (Amendment) Act, No. of 2022.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Bold",
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      161.85,
      316.73,
      401.9,
      365.87
    ],
    "text": "2.The following new section is inserted immediatelyafter section 28 (8) (b) of the Local Authorities ElectionsOrdinance No. 53 of 1946 and shall have effect as section 28(9) in the Principal Enactment:\u2014",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Bold",
      "Times-Italic",
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      168.93,
      379.73,
      401.89,
      466.67
    ],
    "text": "\u201c28 (9)(1) When submitting a nomination paper eachpolitical party and independent group shallensure that not less than one fourth of the totalnumber of candidates to be nominated for thelocal authority, and not less than one fourth ofthe total number of candidates in the districtlist, shall be youth candidates.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      198.57,
      480.53,
      401.89,
      529.67
    ],
    "text": "(2) The Commissioner of Elections shall by noticepublished in the Gazette, specify the numberof youth candidates to be nominated in respectof each local authority.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      198.57,
      543.53,
      401.92,
      605.27
    ],
    "text": "(3) For the purposes of this Clause a youth shallbe defined as an individual either male orfemale of 35 years of age or less on the day ofthe calling of elections by the electionscommissioner.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      198.57,
      619.13,
      401.88,
      668.27
    ],
    "text": "(4) In the event of a failure by a political party tomeet the required condition set our aboveclause 28 (9) (1) with regard to the youth quotafor nominations such nomination paper shall",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      408.81,
      317.11,
      454.54,
      374.18
    ],
    "text": "Amendmentof section 28of the LocalAuthoritiesElectionsOrdinance",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      157.15,
